Fix the texture preload cache on the OpenGL renderer: hang, then untextured table.

The texture loader runs its images through a ThreadPool, and when a texture is
listed in the table's used_textures.xml cache it takes this path:

    #ifdef ENABLE_OPENGL
    // Uploading texture in OpenGL uses the state machine which will be wrong if done concurrently
    const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock2(mutex);
    #endif
    m_renderer->m_renderDevice->UploadTexture(image, linearRGB);
    uploaded = true;

Two problems, one behind the other.

'mutex' is already held a few lines above, for the whole block that follows
GetRawBitmap(), and std::mutex is not recursive: the first worker thread to
reach a cached texture deadlocks on itself while still holding the mutex, and
every other loader thread piles up behind it. VPX hangs during startup, right
after logging:

    INFO  [Player::Player@571] Texture cache found at .../used_textures.xml

The lock is not merely deadlocking, it is also the wrong tool. A mutex
serializes the calls, but it cannot give the worker thread a GL context, and
the context is only ever made current on the main thread. So even serialized,
UploadTexture() from these threads issues its GL calls into nothing. Worse,
'uploaded' is set to true regardless, which skips the AddPendingUpload()
fallback right below, so the image is never registered with the texture manager
either. Every texture listed in the cache -- in practice the whole table --
ends up on the GPU as nothing at all, and the table renders invisible.

Restrict the branch to the backends whose upload is thread safe. On OpenGL,
leaving 'uploaded' false lets the texture manager hold the decoded data and
create the sampler from the main thread on first use, which is what it already
does for every non-cached image. The point of the preload is preserved: the
expensive part (decode and resize) still happens here, in parallel.

Only the OpenGL renderer is affected.

Signed-off-by: Adrien Beudin <beudbeud@gmail.com>

--- a/src/core/player.cpp
+++ b/src/core/player.cpp
@@ -635,12 +635,17 @@
                         const char *name = node->GetText();
                         if (name != nullptr && image->m_name == name && node->QueryBoolAttribute("linear", &linearRGB) == tinyxml2::XML_SUCCESS)
                         {
-                           #ifdef ENABLE_OPENGL
-                           // Uploading texture in OpenGL uses the state machine which will be wrong if done concurrently
-                           const std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock2(mutex);
-                           #endif
+                           #ifndef ENABLE_OPENGL
+                           // OpenGL is excluded here: this runs on the loader thread pool, and the
+                           // GL context is only ever made current on the main thread, so the upload
+                           // would silently do nothing while still flagging the image as uploaded,
+                           // skipping the AddPendingUpload() fallback below and leaving the table
+                           // untextured. Leave 'uploaded' false so the texture manager keeps the
+                           // decoded data and uploads it from the main thread when first needed.
+                           // The costly decode/resize work is still done here, in parallel.
                            m_renderer->m_renderDevice->UploadTexture(image, linearRGB);
                            uploaded = true;
+                           #endif
                            break;
                         }
                      }
